title: "grandpa: don't gossip commits that don't advance finality"
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Gossip an incoming commit only if processing it advanced our view of the finalized height.

    Multiple voters can issue a commit for the same round, and several of them can pass
    validation before any of them is processed, since validation only compares against the
    height noted after processing. Each of them was then gossiped as a separate message, so
    peers received the same finality proof more than once. A commit that doesn't advance our
    finalized height is now dropped after processing instead of being gossiped, and a debug
    log is emitted for it. A commit for that height has already been gossiped.

    The dropped commit is still marked as known (new `GossipEngine::mark_message_known`), so
    later copies of it aren't penalized as past messages.

    Discovered while working on #13318 (but independent of it).
crates:
- name: sc-consensus-grandpa
  bump: patch
- name: sc-network-gossip
  bump: minor
